  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound Qui3Me(b1-4)Oli3Me(a)-O-Et and the CD276 antigen, mediated through Methionine aminopeptidase 2. This compound is identified as a target of two distinct molecular entities, both of which are known to interact with the CD276 antigen. The first molecule, a complex with high confidence scores, directly targets the CD276 antigen, while the second, a more structurally diverse compound, also shows a direct interaction with the CD276 antigen. This indicates that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the CD276 antigen through its interaction with Methionine aminopeptidase 2. The shared pathway through Methionine aminopeptidase 2 provides a consistent mechanism, suggesting that the compound may exert its effects by influencing the activity of this enzyme, which in turn affects the CD276 antigen. The evidence supports a plausible, mechanistic link between the compound and the CD276 antigen, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
